  {
    "id": "basics-21",
    "title": "Stretching tuning",
    "html": "<p>Multiply <code>tuning</code> by a positive dimensionless factor to stretch or compress the entire active pitch space while keeping its root fixed. The change scales degrees, the equave, prime mappings, accidentals, and MOS intervals together; here, <code>102%</code> makes 12edo slightly wider.</p>",
    "props": {
      "source": "{12edo} [0,4,7]===\n{tuning *= 102%} [0,4,7]===",
      "instrument": {
        "type": "patch",
        "patchPreset": "default",
        "oscillatorType": "semisine"
      },
      "gain": 0.35,
      "laneSource": "@tempo(240bpm) @adsr(10ms, 100ms, 70%, 100ms)",
      "simplified": true,
      "rows": 3,
      "editorLabel": "Stretching tuning source"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "features-constructed-scales",
    "title": "Scales from expressions",
    "html": "<p><code>{scale = expression}</code> builds a scale from a container of intervals. Entries become degrees 1 onward; degree 0 remains the root, and the final entry sets the equave. Use square brackets and commas to list the intervals. Expressions can also call scale helpers, as the next example demonstrates.</p>",
    "props": {
      "source": "{scale = [9/8, 5/4, 3/2, 2/1]}\n0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8=",
      "instrument": {
        "type": "patch",
        "patchPreset": "default",
        "oscillatorType": "semisine"
      },
      "gain": 0.35,
      "laneSource": "@tempo(240bpm) @adsr(10ms, 100ms, 70%, 100ms)",
      "simplified": true,
      "rows": 3,
      "editorLabel": "Scales from expressions source"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "features-cps",
    "title": "Combination product sets",
    "html": "<p><code>cps(factors, count)</code> builds a combination product set: it multiplies each combination of the requested number of factors, shifts the lowest product to unison, reduces the intervals into one equave, and sorts them into a scale. Optional arguments set the equave and whether to retain the products' original unity. Try replacing 7 with 11 or changing the combination size.</p>",
    "props": {
      "source": "{scale = cps([1 3 5 7], 2)}\n0 1 2 3 4 5 6=\n{scale = cps([1 3 5 7], 2, 2/1, true)}\n0 1 2 3 4 5 6=",
      "instrument": {
        "type": "patch",
        "patchPreset": "default",
        "oscillatorType": "semisine"
      },
      "gain": 0.35,
      "laneSource": "@tempo(240bpm) @adsr(10ms, 100ms, 70%, 100ms)",
      "simplified": true,
      "rows": 4,
      "editorLabel": "Combination product sets source"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "features-context-assignments",
    "title": "Combined tuning assignments",
    "html": "<p>Separate tuning assignments inside braces with semicolons. This lets you construct a scale and choose its mode in one block. A semicolon inside braces separates assignments; outside braces it is a measure rest.</p>",
    "props": {
      "source": "{scale = cps([1 7 11 13], 2); mode = 4; root = 220Hz}\n0 1 2 3 4 5 6=",
      "instrument": {
